      "writtenOn": "2025-09-22T18:27:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT of making objects inherit from \"RecordableObject\" that looks something like:\n\n```\nclass RecordableObject {\n    // The only way to get the ID so we\u0027re sure anything that we get an ID from gets captured.\n    CaptureID EnsureCaptured(CaptureContext* context) {\n       if id !\u003d kNotRecorded/*0*/ { return id }\n       id \u003d context-\u003eGetNewID()\n       CaptureCreation(context)\n       return id\n    }\n    \n    virtual void CaptureCreation(context) \u003d 0;\n}\n```\n\nThis way the capturing of a specific kind of object stays in the implementation of the object which would limit the growth of this file and make it more likely we update the capture when we update the logic in the object?",
      "revId": "8a9a34ee85b09b562d5c9eb42e402fcae9a7fb70",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fcd65d7_9e92820f",
