      "writtenOn": "2025-09-27T04:06:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We discussed this on Tuesda I think? My plan was that only the queue matters. So if you call buffer map/unmap the buffer gets marked as dirty. Next time you call queue.xxx, if the buffer is referenced and is marked as dirty then it will grab the latest content. I am still pretty confused on your proposal for bindless. Maybe if I understood it I\u0027d see why it\u0027s important this be on device. Maybe destroy is enough to say it belongs on device? What happens if/when we support mult-threaded? I think I assumed there would be one \"real\" queue that\u0027s associated with some per worker GPUQueue object. They all share one actual Queue object and just has to coordinate calling submit shared queue. It\u0027s that shared queue that needs capturing.",
      "parentUuid": "c4901dce_9d200702",
      "revId": "8a9a34ee85b09b562d5c9eb42e402fcae9a7fb70",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
